Z||000014||Cliff D.||05-30-2001||02:16 AM||||I have been trying for a while to replace my '98 firebird with my '85 GT as my daily drive, but the only time I ever have the cash to pay off my negative equity is when the fiero is in pieces. I usually spend the money putting it back together and then can't sell the firebird. It's a circle. Anyway, I think it just might be destiny that the 3800 will end up longitudinally in my parts car (identical '85 GT) with one of those super cool tubular kits. I'll just clean the crap out of the firebird chasis and store it until I can sell it as a roller. I will need help getting the transaxle thing figured out. I keep seeing the word Porsche in the archives. sure hope I win the lotto by then.||||reg||1
Z||000015||ThatRickGuy||05-30-2001||08:02 AM||||if it were 8 months ago all over again, I would forget the 3.2 rebuild and just have gone w/ a 3.4. For the price of the rebuild I could have bought the long block w/ a warenty, had the starter mounted and had cash left over. I'm still debating on the next step. one of these 3:<BR>1. 3.4l w/ turbo (or twin turbo)<BR>2. 3800 sc w/ intercooler<BR>3. 350 built up<P>the final goal being 300 hp and at least 275 ft/lbs reliably.||||reg||1
Z||000016||elfiero||05-30-2001||09:24 AM||||People will always glance at a fiero,but when<BR>you hit the key they hear the gear reduction<BR>starter,then the chevy V8 growls to life!!<BR>It is the greatest look in the world.I've<BR>had people come up to me in parking lots and<BR>almost demand to see the engine.Then you put it in first gear and let the clutch out(all<BR>fieros should have 5spds)and the torque pushes you hard into the seat.you short shift<BR>it all the way to 5th,and without straining,<BR>your over 70mph!.For my money a SBC is the<BR>only way to go! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000017||Butter||05-30-2001||10:20 AM||||My next endevor is to shoot for approximately 400hp in that SBC I got sittin' in my shop.  Then I'm gonna' mount that booger up to another good 4speed that's also in there.  Then I'm gonna stick em' in the middle of that ugly little sleeper I been drivin' and open up the gate and let the horses out.  Why I might even take pictures so's yall can see the herd.  That's what I plan on doin' next time my cradle needs a new baby.||||reg||12
